### Member Auth API – manual test requests (VS Code REST Client / Rider .http)
@base = http://localhost:5155

### 1. Login (seeded demo member)
# @name login
POST {{base}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jdoe",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd!",
  "lob": "DENTAL"
}

### 2. Call the protected endpoint with the access token
GET {{base}}/api/v1/members/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3. Rotate the refresh token
POST {{base}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 4. JWKS – public keys for downstream microservices
GET {{base}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### 5. OIDC-style discovery document
GET {{base}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

### 6. Health
GET {{base}}/health


# =====================================================================================
# Pass-through (BFA) mode — Auth:Mode = PassThrough
#
# The routes are identical; only what happens behind them changes. The BFA forwards the
# body verbatim to Apigee Internal → ARTS, and relays ARTS's status, body and
# allow-listed headers straight back.
# =====================================================================================

### 7. Login through the BFA relay
# Note the correlation id: supply one and it travels to ARTS and comes back on the
# response, so a single id links the Member Portal, BFA, Apigee Internal and ARTS logs.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: local-dev-0001

{
  "username": "jdoe",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd!",
  "lob": "DENTAL"
}

### 8. A field the BFA has never heard of still reaches ARTS
# The body is forwarded byte-for-byte, so "deviceFingerprint" survives the hop even
# though no BFA contract mentions it. Adding a login field needs no BFA release.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jdoe",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd!",
  "lob": "DENTAL",
  "deviceFingerprint": "b7d1f0e2-9a44-4c3e-9f6a-2c1d8e5b7a90"
}

### 9. Refresh through the BFA relay
POST {{base}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "paste-a-token-issued-by-ARTS"
}

### 10. Rejected at the edge — no upstream round trip is spent
# Missing 'password' fails the BFA's shape check and returns 400 without ever touching
# ARTS or incrementing its failed-login counter.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jdoe",
  "lob": "DENTAL"
}
